From: Quinby Janes <qcj2000@columbia.edu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:40:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Build the Genetic Risk Check questionnaire from Hila's
 revised document

- Replace the placeholder /check page with the full questionnaire:
  diagnosis/symptoms, age and stage at first diagnosis, other medical
  information (grouped by organ), and family history.
- Conditional questions: 5a and 6 only appear if not adopted; 5b only if
  5a is yes; 7 only if 6 is yes.
- Result logic follows the document's color coding: red answers are low
  risk, the two green answers (diagnosed at 50-65y AND stage 4-5) count
  only together, and any other answer gives the increased-risk result.
- Low-risk results use the document's adopted / not-adopted sentences;
  increased-risk results start "Given that ..." and list every answer
  the patient gave.
- Summary of answers below the result, flagging the ones that
  contributed to it.
- "For patients" / "For doctors" toggle swaps only the preface
  (link with ?for=doctor to open the doctor version).
- All rules live in src/lib/riskCheck.ts; nothing is recorded.

